conditions . meanwhile , the greedy algorithm gives an upper bound on the average data buffer length , and the pa algorithm derives a lower bound . additionally , the case that su can not get the pu s private information is also discussed . numerical results demonstrate that the greedy algorithm and the pa algorithm can produce effective upper & lower bounds on the average buffer length and give important insights into the performance thereafter . 1 t. zhang , w. chen , z. han , and z. cao , a cross - layer perspective on energy harvesting aided green communications over fading channels , _ ieee trans . veh . 1519 - 1534 , apr . 2015 . r. d. yates and h. m .- doost , energy harvesting receivers : packet sampling and decoding policies , _ ieee j. sel . area comm . 558 - 570 , mar . he , l. zhao , s. zhou , and z. niu , recursive waterfilling for wireless links with energy harvesting transmitters , _ ieee trans . . 1232 - 1241 , mar . x. huang , t. han , and n. ansari , on green energy powered cognitive radio networks , _ ieee commun . surv . & tut . 827 - 842 , 2nd - quar . 2015 . m. usman and i. koo , access strategy for hybrid underlay - overlay cognitive radios with energy harvesting , _ ieee sens . j. _ , vol . 9 , pp . 3164 - 3173 , sept . 2014 k. kulkarni and a. banerjee , stable throughput tradeoffs in cognitive radio networks with cooperating rechargeable nodes , _ proc . ieee wcnc15 _ , new orleans , la , mar . 2015 .
